---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { articleSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import CircleMiniPreview from '../components/CircleMiniPreview.astro';
const title='How to Make a Circle in Minecraft – Step-by-Step Block Guide | VoxelCurve';
const description='Learn how to make a circle in Minecraft using center points, anchors, row segments and symmetry. Includes practical 11×11, 21×21 and 31×31 building examples.';
const canonical='https://voxelcurve.com/how-to-make-a-circle-in-minecraft';
const schemas=[
  breadcrumbSchema([{name:'VoxelCurve',url:'https://voxelcurve.com/'},{name:'How to Make a Circle in Minecraft',url:canonical}]),
  articleSchema({headline:'How to Make a Circle in Minecraft',url:canonical,description})
];
---
<BaseLayout {title} {description} {canonical} type="article" {schemas}>
<section class="resource-hero"><div class="container"><div class="resource-hero-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Builder guide</span><h1>How to Make a Circle in Minecraft</h1><p>A practical construction method for small and large block circles—whether you searched how to make, create or build a circle in Minecraft—without trying to eyeball the curve.</p></div><div class="resource-meta"><span>5 STEPS</span><strong>Center → Segments</strong><small>Practical construction workflow</small></div></div></div></section>
<article class="section guide-article"><div class="container editorial-grid"><aside class="editorial-aside"><div class="section-kicker">Circle build method</div><p>Start from the footprint, establish symmetry, then work row by row.</p><a class="aside-cta" href="/#c-31-thin-1">Open 31×31 blueprint →</a></aside><div class="prose editorial-prose"><h2>1. Choose the outside diameter</h2><p>A 21×21 circle occupies a 21-block-wide square. Odd diameters have one center block; even diameters are centered between the middle four blocks. Decide the footprint before placing your first anchor.</p><h2>2. Mark the center and four anchors</h2><p>From the center, mark the north, south, east and west extremes of the circle. These anchors establish the outside boundary and make symmetry much easier to maintain.</p><h2>3. Build with row segments</h2><p>Do not count individual pixels from an image. Treat every row as one or more horizontal runs. For example, a row might contain two blocks on the left, a gap, and two blocks on the right. VoxelCurve shows the exact columns and center-relative offsets.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Best practice:</strong> complete one quarter or one symmetric row at a time. Mirror it before moving deeper into the curve.</div><h2>4. Check symmetry as you go</h2><p>Every left-side run should have a corresponding right-side run. The same is true for top and bottom halves. If a row looks wrong, fix it immediately instead of carrying the offset into later rows.</p><h2>5. Scale the method for large circles</h2><p>For a 31×31 or larger circle, keep the center marked and use exact segment positions rather than repeatedly recounting from the boundary. This reduces cumulative errors on long walls and arena foundations.</p><h2>Example sizes</h2>
<div class="guide-example-grid">
  <a class="guide-example" href="/#c-11-thin-1"><CircleMiniPreview size={11} /><div><h3>11×11</h3><p>A compact size for wells, towers and decorative builds.</p><span>Open blueprint →</span></div></a>
  <a class="guide-example" href="/#c-21-thin-1"><CircleMiniPreview size={21} /><div><h3>21×21</h3><p>A useful medium footprint for rooms, tower bases and observatories.</p><span>Open blueprint →</span></div></a>
  <a class="guide-example" href="/#c-31-thin-1"><CircleMiniPreview size={31} /><div><h3>31×31</h3><p>A large circle where guided rows save significant counting time.</p><span>Open blueprint →</span></div></a>
</div><h2>Use the interactive blueprint</h2><p><a class="text-link" href="/#c-31-thin-1">Open a 31×31 circle in VoxelCurve →</a></p></div></div></article>
<section class="section related-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-kicker">Related tools</div>
  <h2>Use the method with a live blueprint</h2>
  <div class="related-list">
    <a href="/"><span class="related-index">01</span><div><h3>Circle Generator</h3><p>Generate custom diameters with exact row and segment instructions.</p></div><span class="related-arrow">↗</span></a>
    <a href="/minecraft-circle-chart"><span class="related-index">02</span><div><h3>Circle Chart</h3><p>Compare common circle sizes and block counts before choosing a footprint.</p></div><span class="related-arrow">↗</span></a>
    <a href="/minecraft-dome-generator"><span class="related-index">03</span><div><h3>Dome Generator</h3><p>Extend circular geometry upward into a guided layered roof.</p></div><span class="related-arrow">↗</span></a>
  </div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
